===Etymology 1===
{{PIE word|en|gʷṓws|nobox=1}}
[[Image:Koe in weiland bij Gorssel.JPG|thumb|{{lang|en|A '''cow''' eats [[grass]].}}]]

{{etymon|en|inh|enm>cou>cow|id=Bos taurus|tree=1}}
{{inh+|en|enm|cou}}, {{m|enm|cu}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cū||cow}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*kō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*kōz||cow}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*gʷṓws||cow}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sa|गो}}, {{cog|grc|βοῦς}}, {{cog|fa|گاو|tr=gâv}}), {{cog|lv|govs||cow}}, Proto-Slavic {{m|sla-pro|*govędo}} (Serbo-Croatian {{m|sh|govedo}}, Russian {{m|ru|говядина|t=beef}}, {{cog|sco|coo|t=cow}}, {{cog|frr|ko}}, {{m|frr|kø|t=cow}}, {{cog|fy|ko|t=cow}}, {{cog|nl|koe|t=cow}}, {{cog|nds|Koh|Koh, Koo, Kau|t=cow}}, {{cog|de|Kuh|t=cow}}, {{cog|sv|ko|t=cow}}, {{cog|no|ku|t=cow}}, {{cog|is|kýr|t=cow}}, {{cog|la|bōs|t=ox, bull, cow}} (whence English beef), {{cog|hy|կով|t=cow}}. {{doublet|en|beef}}.

<!--Moved from [[kine]].-->The plural {{m|en|kine}} is from {{inh|en|enm|kyne}}, {{m|enm|kyn}}, {{m|enm|kuin}}, {{m|enm|kiin}}, {{m|enm|kien|t=cows}}, either a double plural of {{cog|enm|ky}}, {{m|enm|kye|t=cows}}, equivalent to modern {{suffix|en|kye|en|pos=noun plural|nocat=1}}, or inherited from {{inh|en|ang|cūna|t=cows', of cows}}, genitive plural of {{m|ang|cū|t=cow}}.

====Noun====
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=en}}
{{en-noun|~|+|cattle|kine|pl4qual=archaic or dialectal}}

# {{senseid|en|female Bos}} {{lb|en|strictly|}} An [[adult]] [[female]] of the [[species]] {{taxfmt|Bos taurus|species}}, especially one that has [[calved]].
#: {{hypo|en|dairy cow|milk cow}}
#: {{cot|en|bull|bullock|calf|heifer|heiferette}}
#: {{ux|en|The whole herd is out to pasture right now — the '''cows''', calves, and heifers are out back, and the bulls are down by the creek.}}
# {{senseid|en|any Bos}} {{lb|en|loosely|or|informal}} Any member of the species {{taxfmt|Bos taurus|species}} regardless of [[sex]] or [[age]], including [[bull]]s and [[calf|calves]].
#: {{syn|en|cattle beast}}<!--using this term avoids using the loose sense of "cow" for males-->
#: {{ux|en|We saw lots of '''cows''' at the farm show, including some surprisingly gigantic bulls.}}
# {{senseid|en|beef}} {{lb|en|uncommon|uncountable}} [[beef|Beef]]: the [[meat]] of cattle as [[food]].
#: {{ux|en|The only meat I eat is '''cow'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|any bovid}} {{lb|en|uncommon}} Any [[bovine]]s or [[bovid]]s generally, including [[yak]]s, [[buffalo]], etc.
# {{senseid|en|female of any of various mammalian species}} {{lb|en|biology}} A female member of other large species of [[mammal]], including the bovines, [[moose]], [[whale]]s, [[seal]]s, [[hippo]]s, [[rhino]]s, [[manatee]]s, and [[elephant]]s.
# {{senseid|en|woman, derogatorily}} {{lb|en|derogatory|UK|Irish|informal}} A [[woman]] considered [[unpleasant]] in some way, particularly one considered [[nasty]], [[stupid]], [[fat]], [[lazy]], or [[difficult]].
#* {{RQ:Orwell Down and Out|chapter=32|passage={{...}} the worst insult to a woman, either in London or Paris, is "'''cow'''"; a name which might even be a compliment, for cows are among the most likeable of animals.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1990|title=[[w:House of Cards (UK TV show)|House of Cards]]|section=Season 1, Episode 2
|passage=''Greville Preston:'' You've been set up, you silly '''cow'''. Now, don't let me hear any more about this unless you have absolute stand-up-in-court proof it's [[kosher]]...<br>''Mattie Storin:'' [[pig|Pig]].}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2014-12-05|author=w:Marina Hyde|title=Childbirth is as awful as it is magical, thanks to our postnatal ‘care’|journal=w:The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2014/dec/05/childbirth-postnatal-care-birth-hospital-cuts|passage=By the time of my third, five months ago, I was a right bossy '''cow''' about what I wanted because I knew the drill. For reasons I shan’t bore you with, I got them to induce me at 39 weeks, at 10am, with the epidural going in first, and it was all a dream. }}
# {{senseid|en|chock}} {{lb|en|mining}} A [[chock]]: a [[wedge]] or [[brake]] used to stop a [[machine]] or [[car]].
#: {{cot|en|dog}}
# {{lb|en|US|military|slang}} A third-year [[cadet]] at [[West Point]].
#* Colonel Red Reeder, ''West Point Second Classman''
#*: An assistant manager, wearing the stripes of a cadet corporal, walked up to Coach Smith. Clint knew him, a '''Cow''' from B-l. What had he done to become so outstanding that the Tacs made him a corporal?
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2023|author=James E Parco; David A Levy; Daphne DePorres|title=Attitudes Aren't Free: A Call to Action|page=242
|passage=When I was a '''cow''' (junior) at West Point, I dated a plebe (freshman), which is considered fraternization in the cadet realm.}}
# {{lb|en|fishing|slang}} A fish that is very large for its species, such as a large [[striped bass]] or large [[bluefin tuna]].

=====Usage notes=====
* The plural {{m|en|cows}} is the normal plural for multiple individuals, while {{m|en|cattle}} is used in a more collective sense. The [[umlaut]] plurals {{m|en|kee}}, {{m|en|kie}}, {{m|en|kine}}, {{m|en|ky}} and {{m|en|kye}} are archaic or dialectal, and are not in common use.

